# spec: set_cnc_presets reads CNC [1.5], writes [1.15] with all four bytes, selecting the preset equal to the current step, then writes [1.5] back as it was, because a [1.15] write switches CNC to the selected preset.
# source: hardware report on firmware 1.8.2-11524+e0f7590: with [1.5] = 0b0001, SETGET [1.15] 0000030a returned 0000030a and left [1.5] at 0b0001; SETGET 0100050a switched [1.5] to 0b0501. The [1.5] reply to the write back is synthetic, following the [steps, step, enabled] layout.
device nc700
call set_cnc_presets 0 3 10
send 01 05 01 00
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 00 01
send 01 0f 02 04 00 00 03 0a
recv 01 0f 03 04 00 00 03 0a
send 01 05 02 02 00 01
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 00 01
result ok
